attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a spine.** Columns 0 to 3, `yjgM` to `tabA`, are carried by 94 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0 to 6% of calls {S1, P}. The model names 57 to 99.6% of them, fewest at column 3, `tabA`, 57% {S1}.

@variable **A variable stretch follows at columns 4 to 7**, `arcA` to `yjgH`, carried by 9 to 85%, all shell {S2}. Then a long spine, columns 8 to 35, `pyrL` to `cysQ`, [[aspartate carbamoyltransferase]] at columns 8 to 10 and [[galactofuranose transport]] at columns 23 to 26 {S3, Q}. The most plastic stretch is columns 44 to 52, in a region of plasticity in 34 to 65% of calls, where a branch of `insQ` runs at column 48 {S6, P}.

@model **The model names about as many genes on the spine columns as on the fork and variable ones**, 92% against 92%, and hesitates less there, 0.31 against 0.36 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 3, `tabA`, is a spine column, at 3.16 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on fork and variable columns.** Columns 71 to 79, `yjfM` to `hflK`, are carried by 29 to 88%, 8 persistent and 1 shell {S12}. The last column is `hflK`, in 29% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 92% of genes**, 0.33 bits on average, perplexity 1.5 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.06 against 0.23 bits, and names fewer genes, 75% against 95% {C}.

